 {"id":"CF-081","title":"P3 — docs/BOARD.md 'Current measured state' is hand-typed: 61 rows/66 events/17 warnings claimed, 66/72/19 measured at 7cf19b0","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"reasoning":"Measured at 7cf19b0 (code-factory-readme's close of CF-065) in a clean canonical checkout, review tick code-factory-review-2026-11-03-15-39-07: docs/BOARD.md:43 says \"61 task rows, 66 events, RESULT: OK (17 warning(s))\" and line 46 says \"PASS 61/61 rows parse\"; the same tree carries 66 task rows and 72 events, boardctl prints \"RESULT: OK (19 warning(s))\", and selftest prints \"PASS 66/66 rows parse\". The block is headed \"Current measured state\" and is pinned by hand to d4eec41.\n\nNot a one-off slip — the block has been hand-corrected twice today and drifted both times: a5e7754 set it to 60 rows/64 events at e21f2ce, 91f3a64 corrected it to 61/66 at d4eec41, and it was stale again within four commits (199e5dd filed CF-076, 4b5daa3 filed CF-077, 7bcfab0/7cf19b0 filed and closed with CF-078..CF-080 plus README work — none touched the block). Nothing in the gate derives or compares these counters: tests/selftest.sh's board arm counts rows-parse and prints the live number, and no arm reads docs/BOARD.md. The disclaimer \"Re-run both commands before quoting these numbers\" documents the drift instead of preventing it; a stranger quoting the block gets numbers that are wrong by 5 rows and 6 events, the same class CF-013/CF-033/CF-054 closed for the README status table.\n\nThe repair is a guard, not another number: derive rows and events from the board in a committed check, compare against the block, and fail naming the block and both values — with a red arm proving a deliberately wrong count fails.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Reproduce at the current tip, from the repository root: the row's probe prints the doc's pair different from the measured pair and then the literal line \"DRIFT: docs/BOARD.md measured-state block is stale\" (at 7cf19b0: doc=61 66