+{"id":"CF-085","title":"Satellite lanes inherit repo_url from their primary at mint time, so repointing the primary leaves the whole family on a phantom local: root — validate the root and fan the change out","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-03T16:23:35Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T16:23:35Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"13676ebbb517d73fecf822ebffce11668b12597762cf3e2bb563295596c32f24"},"reasoning":"HYPOTHESIS (root cause not proven this tick): five code-factory-duckbrain satellites (-dogfood -pm -qa -releng -sync) carried repo_url local:/home/kara/code-factory-duckbrain, a path that does not exist (git -C => No such file or directory), while the primary code-factory-duckbrain and every other code-factory satellite carry local:/home/kara/code-factory. Satellite minting inherits the primary repo_url (scripts/add_family_lanes.py:73 and scripts/configure_family.py:163 hard-code the correct ROOT, so an older mint or an inherited-then-repointed primary is the likely mechanism); nothing fans a primary repoint out to its satellites, and no path validates that the registered root is a git root. Effect: every tick of those five lanes was identity-BLOCKED (lane history for -sync: 11 ticks, 1 committed / 8 dry_run / 2 failed). Repaired 2026-11-03 by partial PUT of repo_url plus the fleet.toml line (5 lines, diff scoped) — this row tracks the durable guard, not the repair. Fleet-wide measured class from the same scan: 307 of 790 local: repo_url rows resolve to a path that is not a git root (242 of them stand-in class), 12 rows point at paths that do not exist at all (python-audit-* family, mischief-chaos, ai-plays-poke).","acceptance_criteria":"A repo check rejects a project row whose local: repo_url does not resolve to a git root (git -C <path> rev-parse --show-toplevel must equal <path>) with a named error and a non-zero exit, a test in tests/ proves the phantom case fails while the real root passes, and the documented reconciliation repoints every satellite of a primary whose repo_url changed; verified by bash tests/selftest.sh exiting 0 with the new case listed and scripts/boardctl validate printing RESULT: OK.","capability_tags":["fleet","config","validation"]}
